## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about 3-valued semantics in robotics sensor fusion and implement a concrete propagator for arbitrary rule sets.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic (T>U>F)
- Propagation rules for ¬, ∧, ∨, and → (X→Y ≡ ¬X ∨ Y)
- Backtracking to avoid F while preserving at least one U

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple 3-valued implication using Kleene logic
function implies(x, y){
  const not = v => v === 'T' ? 'F' : v === 'F' ? 'T' : 'U';
  const or = (a,b) => (a==='T' || b==='T') ? 'T' : (a==='U' || b==='U') ? 'U' : 'F';
  return or(not(x), y);
}
```

